  "description": "ADO-PARAM against connection changes: a Command on 'SELECT ID, Code FROM T WHERE L = ?' with ActiveConnection cn1 and a refreshed Parameters inventory; ActiveConnection set by reference to a second open Connection (State, inventory, Parameters(0) = 20, Execute and rows); the first Connection closed (State, ActiveConnection, inventory, Execute); the second closed (inventory, Refresh, Execute and the second's Errors); ActiveConnection set to a third Connection that was never opened (State, Execute, inventory). Asks what the Command and its collection keep when its connection changes or closes.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
